facts:
$\tfrac{1}{2} = \tfrac{2}{4} = \tfrac{3}{6} = \tfrac{5}{10}$ — all the same amount.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\fill[gray!40] (0,0) rectangle (2,0.8);
\draw (0,0) rectangle (4,0.8);
\draw (2,0) -- (2,0.8);
\node[right] at (4.25,0.4) {$\frac{1}{2}$};
\fill[gray!40] (0,-1.4) rectangle (2,-0.6);
\draw (0,-1.4) rectangle (4,-0.6);
\foreach \x in {1,2,3} {\draw (\x,-1.4) -- (\x,-0.6);}
\node[right] at (4.25,-1) {$\frac{2}{4}$};
\fill[gray!40] (0,-2.8) rectangle (2,-2);
\draw (0,-2.8) rectangle (4,-2);
\foreach \x in {0.6666,1.3333,2,2.6666,3.3333} {\draw (\x,-2.8) -- (\x,-2);}
\node[right] at (4.25,-2.4) {$\frac{3}{6}$};
\fill[gray!40] (0,-4.2) rectangle (2,-3.4);
\draw (0,-4.2) rectangle (4,-3.4);
\foreach \x in {0.4,0.8,1.2,1.6,2,2.4,2.8,3.2,3.6} {\draw (\x,-4.2) -- (\x,-3.4);}
\node[right] at (4.25,-3.8) {$\frac{5}{10}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

workedExamples.question_text:
The equal-length bars show the same shaded amount.
(a) Write the fraction shaded in the top bar.
(b) Group every $5$ small parts into one larger part. Write the equivalent fraction shown by the bottom bar.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}
\fill[gray!40] (0,0) rectangle (4,0.8);
\draw[black] (0,0) rectangle (6,0.8);
\foreach \i in {1,...,14} {\draw[black] ({\i*0.4},0)--({\i*0.4},0.8);}
\fill[gray!40] (0,-1.6) rectangle (4,-0.8);
\draw[black] (0,-1.6) rectangle (6,-0.8);
\foreach \x in {2,4} {\draw[black] (\x,-1.6)--(\x,-0.8);}
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

